WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:01.001
Bill Gates.

00:00:01.084 --> 00:00:02.419
-Your favorite animal?
-Dog.

00:00:02.503 --> 00:00:03.962
-Your favorite food?
-Hamburger.

00:00:04.046 --> 00:00:05.297
-Eat breakfast?
-Nothing.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.924
What is your worst fear?

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.969
I don't want my brain
to stop working.

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:14.515
Bill is a multiprocessor.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.391
He'll be reading
something else

00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:18.227
but then processing
at the same time.

00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:20.062
It's chaos!

00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:23.398
He thrives on complexity.

00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:25.108
He makes a framework
in his mind

00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:28.028
and then he starts
slotting in the information.

00:00:28.612 --> 00:00:31.823
If something doesn't line up,
he gets really frustrated.

00:00:31.907 --> 00:00:33.325
It's scary.

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:35.369
But when Bill stills himself,

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:38.664
he can pull ideas together
that other people can't see.

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:43.210
At Microsoft,
I worked night and day.

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:45.504
That was how I made sure
Microsoft stayed ahead.

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:47.256
I could be so extreme.

00:00:47.339 --> 00:00:49.716
You never understood
the first thing about this!

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.427
Microsoft hit a new
record high on Wall Street.

00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:54.930
Rivals paint a dark picture.

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:58.141
He'll do whatever he can
to capture more of the market.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.935
Our mother wanted him
to focus

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:02.020
on community and family.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:05.607
I gave my mom a hard time
not following what she wanted.

00:01:05.691 --> 00:01:07.109
You don't raise a family

00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:08.986
hyper-focused in your head.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.071
Each one of us has to start out

00:01:11.154 --> 00:01:14.992
with developing his or her
own definition of success.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.205
I had the wrong way
of looking at things.

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:25.377
In life, you have to decide,
what's important in the world?

00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:28.714
I will look at energy,
climate change,

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:31.758
and disease eradication.

00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:35.345
It's important that we start
deploying solutions

00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:36.805
unnaturally fast.

00:01:38.181 --> 00:01:39.766
We are running out&nbsp;
of time here.

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:44.354
He tends to look at problems
from unusual angles.

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:47.941
There hasn't been innovation
in nuclear energy for 25 years.

00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:51.612
What are the odds
of getting the job done?

00:01:52.696 --> 00:01:54.698
If you want to make
a dent in this,

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.409
you better think
in wholesale magnitudes.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:58.619
He's at his best

00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:00.871
when the deck is stacked
against him.

00:02:02.247 --> 00:02:03.832
There's many challenges.

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:05.751
This is harder than I expected.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.337
Ultimately,
it's not what you get...

00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:13.300
it's what you become.

